X-SOURCE-ID:trumba_calendars_buncombe_county_government_ics
X-SOURCE:Buncombe County Government
SUMMARY:Buncombe County Parks Update - Open and Closed Parks
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260914
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260915
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-ALLDAYEVENT:TRUE
X-TRUMBA-CUSTOMFIELD;NAME="Event Type";ID=21;TYPE=number:Park &amp\; Rec
 reation
X-TRUMBA-CUSTOMFIELD;NAME="Email";ID=35519;TYPE=Email:<a href="mailto:pa
 rks@buncombecounty.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">parks@buncombecou
 nty.org</a>
X-TRUMBA-CUSTOMFIELD;NAME="Phone";ID=35516;TYPE=PhoneUS10NoExt:(828) 250
 -4260
X-TRUMBA-CUSTOMFIELD;NAME="Notice - Description";ID=51963;TYPE=SingleLin
 e:Information about Open and Closed Parks
DTSTAMP:20250617T085331Z
DESCRIPTION:Email: parks@buncombecounty.org<br>Phone: (828) 250-4260<br>
 Notice - Description: Information about Open and Closed Parks<br><br>Man
 y Buncombe County Parks were impacted by Hurricane Helene.&#160\; While 
 we are working diligently reopen parks as quickly as we can\, some parks
  continue to remain closed. Please see the list below for which parks ar
 e open and which parks continue to be closed for safety reasons.<br><br>
 OPEN Parks:&#160\; Lake Julian Park (please note\, some disc golf holes 
 remain closed)\, Hominy Valley Park\, Collier Cove Nature Preserve\, Nor
 th Buncombe Fields\, Cane Creek Playground\, Buncombe County Sports Park
 \, Corcoran Paige River Park\, Bent Creek River Park\, Ledges Whitewater
  Park\, and Hominy Creek River Park.&#160\; If people choose to recreate
  on the river\, we strongly encourage them to be aware of changes on str
 eambanks and in the riverbed and the potential for unknown debris from H
 elene.<br><br>CLOSED Parks:&#160\; Charles D. Owen Park\, Karpen Soccer 
 Field\, Alexander River Park\, Walnut Island River Park\, and Glen Bridg
 e River Park*. *Note\, if the gate is open at Glen Bridge River Park\, i
 t may be used.&#160\; For safety reasons\, we ask the public not to ente
 r closed parks.<br><br>Please email <a href="mailto:parks@buncombecounty
 .org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">parks@buncombecounty.org</a> or cal
 l (828) 250-4260 with any questions or for additional information.
CATEGORIES:Parks &amp; Recreation
UID:http://uid.trumba.com/event/179136486
X-TRUMBA-LINK:https://www.buncombecounty.org/countycenter/events-calenda
 r.aspx?trumbaEmbed=view%3Devent%26eventid%3D179136486
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Ashevillehikinggroup": "https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/316502096/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_ashevillehikinggroup
X-SOURCE:Asheville Hiking Group
UID:event_316502096@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260913T043019Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260914T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260914T140000
SUMMARY:Sam's Gap to Rice Gap 7.5 Mi\, 1700 Ft EG
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nWe are headed off in a different d
 irection this week and it about 30 minutes north from the carpool meetup l
 ocation. It is a nice out and back section of the AT starting at Sam's Gap
  and turning around at Rice Gap. The hike will be a total of 7.5 miles\, 1
 700 ft of elevation gain and reach about 4500 ft elevation. We will pass H
 igh Rock and stop at the Hog Back Shelter for a quick lunch on the way bac
 k. There is a custom AllTrails link below. This is a bit of a longer hike 
 with some decent elevation gain so be prepared for a longer day.\n\nhttps:
 //www.alltrails.com/explore/custom-routes/uploaded-route-a0047c1\n\n**CARP
 OOL**\nMeet behind the Earth Fare by the Tesla chargers in WestGate Plaza 
 at 8am. If you want to go directly to the trailhead\, please let me know a
 nd use the directions in AllTrails.\n\n**WEATHER**\nAs usual the weather i
 s a bit uncertain for Monday but I'll watch the weather and post a cancell
 ation message by 7:00 AM if there is a chance of severe weather or lightni
 ng during this time period..\n\n**QUESTIONS?**\nYou can message me through
  MeetUp until 8:00 AM the day of. Cell reception may be sketchy\, but you 
 can try to text or call me up to the start of the hike: (508) 965-2333.\n\
 n**LEGALESE**\nThis Asheville Hiking Group event involves hiking and\, pos
 sibly\, transportation to and from the meetup site. Participants are respo
 nsible for their own safety and affirm that they have the appropriate skil
 ls\, physical conditioning\, equipment\, and supplies. Hiking may involve 
 risks to oneself and property. Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville H
 iking Group can assure your safety nor eliminate all risks. Participants a
 ssume full responsibility for any injuries\, damages\, or losses.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/316502096
 /
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260910T175857Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260910T175857Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
