SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260913T043038Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260917T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260917T150000
SUMMARY:Grandfather Mtn\; a challenge.
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nWe are the **Sloth Hike Team of WNC**: “W
 e will get there when we get there.” We dare to go where the ‘real’ 
 hike groups don’t ***!!***\n**John Muir didn’t like the word ‘hike
 ’. *“We ought to saunter through them reverently\, not 'hike' through 
 them.”***\nI am going to Grandfather Mtn Park\; Up to 8 ppl are welcome 
 to join me.\n**Hike Distance: 2.0 mi total Accum ascent: 400 ft\; Elevatio
 n: 5000 ft.** Trail map in photos below.\nPace: **1.0mph – because I’m
  an ol’ Codger.**\n**Difficulty: All of the trail is large rock - most i
 s climbing.**\n**Masticating will be ‘in motion’.**\nDrive time: 1.5 h
 rs/ 77 mi 1-way. (arrive 10am)\n**Return Not earlier than: 2:30p (=6.0 hrs
 )**\n***Carpool contributions appreciated. $10.00 suggested***\n***Park Ad
 mission Fee: $30 per person.***\nWeather Check: Blowing Rock\, NC\nhttps:/
 /www.mountain-forecast.com/peaks/Grandfather-Mountain/forecasts/latest\nWe
 ather cancellations will be posted the evening before.\nWAITLISTED PEOPLE 
 WILL BE ADDED AS DRIVERS SIGN ON.\nI currently have 3 driver(s) (=12ppl)\n
 We suggest slightly open windows while carpooling. Only you know your own 
 health status so judge accordingly if an event may endanger your health or
  the health of others.\nPlease bring an extra pair of shoes to avoid bring
 ing your muddy shoes into the driver's car at the end of the hike.\n**I do
  *NOT* suggest bringing Fluffy on this event**\n**DESCRIPTION\;**\nRemembe
 r - hikes led by ‘the Curmudgeon’ tend to have challenging surprises.\
 nMountain Trolls are thieves\; Zip your backpacks tight.\nWe will park at 
 the Hikers Parking area and hike the Grandfather Ext trail (0.6mi) to the 
 Grandfather Trail (0.5mi) to the Swinging bridge. Then returned on the 'Br
 idge trail' (0.4mi). **Several steep sections (400 ft accum ascent).** All
  of the trail is large rock - most is climbing.\n**The Bridge Trail:** wal
 k through rhododendron\, galax\, red spruce\, Fraser fir\, and yellow birc
 h. 0.4 mile on switchbacks down the mountain\, passing under the Swinging 
 Bridge. You'll be awed by the massive rock outcroppings on this trail.\nAl
 l hikes are at your own risk. You are responsible for your OWN safety and 
 adequate equipment.\nWaiver: : The organizer of this event is a volunteer 
 and not a professional guide. The function of the organizer is only to org
 anize this event. There are certain risks inherent in any outdoor activity
 . Each participant\, by signing up to attend this event\, agrees to releas
 e from liability the leader(s)\, Hendo Fun Friends\, its Partners\, Affili
 ates\, and members for any accident\, injury\, illness\, or personal loss 
 which might occur while participating in this activity or while traveling 
 in any vehicle during this trip. **Each participant further agrees to abid
 e by the rules and regulations concerning safety\, to follow instructions 
 of the leader(s)\, and not to become intentionally separated from the grou
 p.** The leader(s) also has the right to use any images collected on this 
 trip for recording on website photo collections.\ngordie's contact: Curmud
 geonHiker@gmail.com\n(**before** day of hike): 828.393.0297 (text only)\n*
 *Pics: https://www.flickr.com/photos/146993931@N05/albums**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/https-www-meetup-com-hendo-fun-friend
 s/events/315973370/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260804T112446Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260804T112446Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
