X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Warren Wilson College": "https://events.warren-wilson.edu/event/sister-sadie-the-kittredge-arts-center-grand-reopening", "Asheville.com": "https://www.asheville.com/event/sister-sadie-the-kittredge-arts-center-grand-reopening", "Hendersonville.com": "https://www.hendersonville.com/event/sister-sadie-the-kittredge-arts-center-grand-reopening"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Calendar Ics": "https://events.warren-wilson.edu/event/sister-sadie-the-kittredge-arts-center-grand-reopening"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_calendar_ics
X-SOURCE:Warren Wilson College, Asheville.com, Hendersonville.com
DTSTAMP:20260913T043059Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53886473896943
DTSTART:20261002T230000Z
DTEND:20261003T003000Z
DESCRIPTION:On Friday October 2nd at 7 PM\, Warren Wilson College celebrate
 s the grand reopening of Kittredge Arts Center\, with renowned Bluegrass a
 ct Sister Sadie headlining!  The Kittredge Arts Center grand reopening is 
 part of the Warren Wilson College's 2026 Homecoming\, and is also a homeco
 ming for Sister Sadie's mandolinist\, WWC alum' Rainy Miatke (Music Major\
 , Class of 2025).\n\n \n\n \n\nTickets can be purchased here:  https://wwc
 -ventures.ticketspice.com/sister-sadie-and-the-kittredge-arts-center-grand
 -reopening \n\n \n\nFor more information abuot the event\, please contact 
 Dr. Jason DeCristofaro at jdecristofaro@warren-wilson.edu or (828)545-3916
 .  \n\n \n\n \n\nSister Sadie Bio:\n\nWhat started as an accidental band b
 ecame a force. GRAMMY-nominated. IBMA-decorated. Opry-validated. But for a
 ll the\naccolades\, they were often reduced to one line: an all-female blu
 egrass band. True—but never the point. Sister Sadie has always\nbeen abo
 ut the music. The fire. The truth.\n\n\nTheir new album\, All Will Be Well
 \, is that truth—loud\, fearless\, and free. You’ll hear echoes of blu
 egrass\, but what rises is\nsomething bigger: country with claws\, America
 na with muscle\, gospel grit and raw storytelling.\n\n\nFrom the haunting 
 “Prodigal Daughter” to the swagger of “Do What You Want” and the a
 ching beauty of “If I Don’t Have You\,”\nthese six women are not per
 forming roles—they’re telling you who they are.\n\n\nThis is Sister Sa
 die\, evolved: bold\, bonded\, and braver than ever. They're not asking fo
 r space. They're taking it.\n\n\nAnd they’re just getting started.\n\n \
 n\nAbout Kittredge Arts Center:\n\nNestled within the beautiful\, historic
  Warren Wilson College campus\, the Kittredge Arts Center provides a centr
 alized location for the arts at WWC and WNC. The Center features the 321-s
 eat Kittredge Theater and 80-seat Williams Recital Hall\, where music and 
 performance events are featured throughout the year. Kittredge Arts Center
  is also available as a rental space to organizations looking for an affor
 dable option in a beautiful location for conferences\, business retreats\,
  and other events. \n\n \n\nFor more information\, please contact Dr. Jaso
 n DeCristofaro (Assistant Professor of Music\, Music Department Chair\, an
 d Director of Kittredge Arts Center) at 828-545-3916 or jdecristofaro@warr
 en-wilson.edu
GEO:35.613818;-82.438862
LOCATION:Kittredge Arts Center\, Kittredge Theater
